},
{
"id": "B1",
"name": "chase around a corner: after losing sight it stays a chase (HUNTING, at pursuit speed) at least until the predicted route is checked or it sees the prey again; it never turns CURIOUS",
"ok": false,
"note": "16 chases lost round a corner (the prey running on): kept the chase in 8; saw the prey again within 3 s in 10; mean speed in the first 1.5 s (lunge recovery excluded) 170 px/s (chase 292); reached the last-seen spot 100% (runs not re-seen); CURIOUS in 8; pursuit sources -; states HUNTING, CURIOUS"
},
{
"id": "B3",
"name": "recent running out of sight updates the pursuit: followed by ear, the chase kept, its goal nearer the real prey than when the prey goes on quietly; the goal moves far less than the steps' blur (no per-footstep jitter)",
"ok": false,
"note": "14 paired chases (same seed; out of sight the prey runs on, or creeps on quietly): followed by ear in 0%; the pursuit goal was 219 px from a running prey vs 193 px from a quiet one (closer in 57%); CURIOUS 8; largest jump of the ear goal between ticks 0 px, against 0 px between the raw heard steps (the steps' blur)"
},
{
"id": "B2",
"name": "a silent change of route fools it: the predicted route continues the heading it saw, away from where the prey really went",
"ok": false,
"note": "12 chases where the prey, out of sight, crept back the way it came: the Hound planned a predicted route in 0, ahead along the heading it saw in 0%, i.e. farther from the real prey than the spot where it vanished in 0%; the prey stayed unseen for 6 s in 25% (the rest were seen on the way to that spot)"
},
